[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:25. Do the English Speak English]
[00:00.680]Passage 25 | 文章二十五
[00:02.855]Do the English speak English? | 英国人说英语吗？
[00:07.090]I arrived in London at last. | 我终于抵达伦敦。
[00:11.110]The railway station was big, black and dark. | 火车站又大、又黑、又暗。
[00:15.630]I did not know the way to my hotel, so I asked a porter. | 我不知道去饭店的路，就问了一个搬运工人。
[00:20.670]I not only spoke English very carefully, but very clearly as well. | 我不但讲英语非常认真，而且讲得非常清楚。
[00:27.405]The porter, however, could not understand me. | 然而，那个搬运工人听不懂我的话。
[00:31.155]I repeated my question several times, and at last he understood. | 我把我的问题重复了几遍，他最后才听懂了。
[00:37.315]He answered me, but he spoke neither slowly nor clearly. | 他回答我，可他讲得既不慢又不清楚。
[00:43.300]‘I am a foreigner,’ I said. | “我是个外国人。”我说。
[00:47.275]Then he spoke slowly, but I could not understand him. | 于是他讲慢了，但我还是听不懂他。
[00:52.660]My teacher never spoke English like that. | 我的老师从来不像他那样讲英语。
[00:56.385]The porter and I looked at each other and smiled. | 那个搬运工和我互相对视了一下，都笑了。
[01:01.960]Then he said something and I understood it. | 后来他又说了些什么，我听懂了。
[01:06.565]‘You’ll soon learn English,’ he said. | “你很快就会学会英语的。”他说。
[01:10.930]I wonder. | 我在想，
[01:13.090]In England each man speaks a different language. | 在英国每个人都说不同的语言。
[01:17.810]The English understand each other, but I don’t understand them. | 英国人彼此都能听懂，可我听不懂他们。
[01:23.770]Do they speak English? | 他们说的是英语吗？